#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/manage-repeated-key-presses.md:0
msgid ""
"Control how a key repeats when you hold it down on Ubuntu Desktop by turning "
"repeat keys off or changing the delay and speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/manage-repeated-key-presses.md:7
msgid "Topics: Accessibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/manage-repeated-key-presses.md:11
msgid "Manage repeated key presses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/manage-repeated-key-presses.md:13
msgid ""
"By default, when you hold down a key on your keyboard, the letter or symbol "
"will be repeated until you release the key. If you have difficulty picking "
"your finger back up quickly enough, you can disable this feature, or change "
"how long it takes before key presses start repeating, or how quickly key "
"presses repeat."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/manage-repeated-key-presses.md:15
msgid "Open the Activities overview and start typing **accessibility**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/manage-repeated-key-presses.md:16
msgid "Click {guilabel}`Accessibility` to open the panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/manage-repeated-key-presses.md:17
msgid "Open the {guilabel}`Typing` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/manage-repeated-key-presses.md:18
msgid ""
"In the {guilabel}`Typing Assist` section, enable the {guilabel}`Repeat Keys` "
"option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/manage-repeated-key-presses.md:19
msgid ""
"Alternatively, adjust the {guilabel}`Delay` slider to control how long you "
"have to hold a key down to begin repeating it, and adjust the {guilabel}"
"`Speed` slider to control how quickly key presses repeat."
msgstr ""
